WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.667
-It is always so great to see you.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.667
Gosh, that was so fun. -Oh, my. Isn't he the best?

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.300
-The two of you -- Everyone -- Together.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.300
It's was the most fun thing ever.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.167
I just also love how we know each other now so well

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.501
that you're like,

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.834
"That's very cool, but it's too cool for you."

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:16.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.067
And you were right. I'm like, "Yeah, you're right."

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:20.968
-No, well, I just -- I feel like you and Noah --

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.734
same person to me.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.400
Like, you guys are just the same person.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.501
You guys just -- Same energy, same vibe.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:29.367
Noah's not cool enough to get a call from LeBron James.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.033
-Yeah, no, he's not... -He's not.

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:34.133
-You brought a picture of you and Eeyore.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.133
-Yes. That's my rabbit. [ Audience awws ]

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.334
-I mean, stop.

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:39.000
And you think this is the cutest thing ever,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.868
but then you brought another one to top this cute.

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:44.100
This is you and your dog and your bunny in bed together.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.801
-Yes. Hugging.

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:48.000
[ Audience awws ] Yeah.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.901
He, uh -- He is a genius.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:54.200
And like I said, he buzzes when he gets really happy.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.534
So he'll just -- Right behi-- He'll come up to me,

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.601
and I'll be going to work, and he'll look at me. "Bzz!"

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.767
And I'll be like, "Alright. Like, he's coming with me."

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.267
I pick him up put him in his stroller,

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:05.434
push him onto set, and it's, like, the best life.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:07.300
-You -- I'm sorry. Wait. You put him in his stroller?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.601
-Yeah.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.334
-You put him in his stroller and stroll him on set?

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.467
-Yes. Car seat and all. It's a situation. Yeah.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:17.100
-We talked about this last time you were on the show.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.667
We were talking about, is there anyone surprising

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.200
that loves you from "Stranger Things"?

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.334
And you're like, "Lots of people. It's crazy."

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.901
'Cause, I mean, everyone loves you and loves the show.

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.968
But Mariah Carey's son loved you so much

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.634
and Mariah Carey loves you,

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:33.200
and they carved you into a pumpkin.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.834
-Yeah, I saw this and thought -- Oh --

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.334
And, by the way, love Mariah,

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:38.901
but, like, her son is the cutest thing ever.

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:41.334
I was like, "Oh, I need to meet her son..."

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.501
and, you know, do the pose

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.934
and, like, make him think that I have superpowers.

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:50.067
And we met -- And Monroe and Moroccan --

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:52.167
who are just the most brilliant little children.

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.968
And then, obviously, I just, like, met Mariah

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.133
and was just like, "Oh."

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.167
Like, we connected. It was just like a --

00:01:58.167 --> 00:01:59.534
-You connected with Mariah Carey?

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.300
-Yeah. "Mimi."

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:06.334
-Does Mimi ever text you? -We texted today.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:08.467
Oh, yeah, she called me today. Oh, yeah.

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:10.801
-Are we still playing the game or is this real?

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:15.601
-No, I -- I mean, we're -- The reason is because

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.734
she grew up, you know, in the public eye,

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:22.334
and we have connected just on so many different levels.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.000
But also I love the way

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.801
that she leads her life with so much power,

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:31.901
and she has so much knowledge and she's so wise.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:34.467
And she's just been an incredible guiding light for me.

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:37.200
And then we connected, and then I go over to her house

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.000
and I'll be, like, eating dinner,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.567
and she'll come around and she'll be like --

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:41.934
[ Harmonizing ]

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.367
I'll be like...

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.133
-No, for real?! -No, it's a real thing.

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:46.767
It's not like -- People are like --

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:47.901
No, no, no, no, no.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.300
She does it when we're eating Chinese food.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.534
-Wait! What?! -It's wild.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:53.000
-She's coming on. I want to talk to her about this.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.968
-Oh, yeah, but don't -- Yeah. -She just has to do it?

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:57.100
-Oh, no, she'll just do it, and you're just kind of like --

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.000
And she'll just be talking to you and she's like...

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.367
♪ Always be my baby ♪

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:03.033
-You'll be like, "You just said that?"

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:05.534
-I'm like, "Hold on." -Wait. So you guys are buds?

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:07.567
-Buds. -Do you ever sing with her?

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:10.100
-We have sung together, yeah, yeah.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.767
-Have you ever -- Like, for real --

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:14.767
-Like, in her studio, sung together.

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:16.734
-What?! -Yeah!

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:19.400
-Wait! Is there something --

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.667
Could something be in the works? -Potentially.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.934
I mean, there's always -- She's always doing something.

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.968
She's, like, the most -- the busiest woman ever.

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:28.300
I call her, and she's in the middle of, like, changing the --

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.567
I'm like, "Oh, hold on one second. Can we talk?"

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:31.968
She's like, "Oh, one second, darling.

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:34.234
I'm performing at MSG." I'm like, "I'm sorry?"

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:36.434
-Yeah, exactly. -It's the most incredible --

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.567
-And I'm just like, "Can we hang out?"

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.367
And then I'll just go over, and we'll sing together.

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:41.534
It's the most magical.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:44.534
She is the most talented singer ever.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:47.300
-Mariah Carey and Millie Bobby Brown -- maybe a collab?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.767
-Potentially. I don't know. [ Laughter ]

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:52.167
-This is the biggest scoop I've ever gotten

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:53.868
on "The Tonight Show" ever. I love it.

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:55.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.901
I would buy that in two seconds. I cannot wait.

00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:00.901
Again, I don't want to take credit

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.567
for anyone's career, besides LeBron James,

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:06.968
but when you were here for "Enola Holmes,"

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:09.467
the first one, I was like -- I went in the dressing room.

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:11.734
I'm like, "Millie, I absolutely love this.

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:14.467
It is a smash. It is a hit. I think this is the b--"

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.767
And you're like, "Oh, really? Bah-bah-bah."

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:18.667
And it became the biggest thing in the world

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.234
I feel like because I put that vibe out there.

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:22.634
-You manifested it, Jimmy.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:24.934
-I did, right? It's so funny. It is so good.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:26.767
It's well-written. It's charming.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:28.667
So now you're back with "2." -I am.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.033
-"Enola Holmes 2." -I am.

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:32.367
-November 4th. Next Friday.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.467
[ Cheers and applause ] -Yeah.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.968
-And you're producing this, as well.

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.334
-Yes. -I mean, this is just

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.467
the best thing ever. -It really is.

00:04:40.467 --> 00:04:43.200
This is something that I have been wanting to do

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.234
since I was little -- I mean, 13, 14.

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.567
I read the book series, and I went to my dad

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:48.934
and said I wanted to make it.

00:04:48.934 --> 00:04:51.501
So for me, my older sister and I have

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:53.400
collaborated on this project

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.934
and made sure that it came to light in the most authentic

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.133
and British way as possible.

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:00.901
And, you know, I never had, growing up,

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:03.467
a female British lead to look up to.

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:05.133
And Enola is that for me.

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:08.000
And it's been an amazing experience creating it.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.868
-You were saying to me, like, so many little girls --

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.567
That's, like, one of the coolest parts of this.

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.234
Little girls coming up to you and going like --

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:16.033
Or parents going, "My daughter is obsessed with Enola Holmes."

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:17.767
-It's so funny, and I'll be like --

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.501
You know, they'll be like, "Can you say it?"

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.634
And I'm like, "'Tis I." And they're like, "Aah!"

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.767
But it's so fun because,

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:25.901
you know, there will be kids that are doing their little --

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:27.501
They're American, and they're doing their

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.033
little English accent, and they're like,

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.267
"My brother Sherlock Holmes."

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.734
I'll be like, "Oh, God." I love it.

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.267
It's just the most incredible feeling.

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:36.167
I mean, Blake Lively -- she text me once.

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:38.534
I mean, I know that you're... You know of them.

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:40.133
-Oh, Blake. Are you kidding me?

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.367
She calls me. -She calls you.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:43.367
We're not on a calling basis at all.

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:45.667
-We're over texting. We want to go voice-to-voice.

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.534
-One conversation... -Walkie-talkie.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.100
-Bedroom-to-bedroom. "Hey, you there?"

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.434
-Flashing mirrors back and forth like, "Hi, Blake."

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:54.801
-Morse code. -Yeah.

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:57.434
-No. I was like -- You know, she's like, "Hey, listen.

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:59.601
My daughter wants to wear --

00:05:59.601 --> 00:06:02.601
to basically just live in an Enola Holmes costume."

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:05.234
And I was like, "Well, I don't have any for you."

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:08.367
And she was like, "How can I get a dress that looks like it?

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.567
Because she wants to be Enola just for her life."

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:12.801
And I was like, "Okay, well, maybe go on Etsy,

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:14.000
type in '1800 dresses.'"

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.434
Because I can't even get the dresses. She wants --

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:18.601
And I was like, "You don't want to wear --"

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:20.400
I was like, "Let her know she doesn't want to wear the dress.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.767
These are corseted." -So you have at least --

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:25.000
You have at least two Halloween costumes.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.634
People are dressing as you for Halloween. Three probably.

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:30.534
-Now I just stay in, Halloween. -You don't even leave the house.

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:32.200
-My little sister's like, "Can you c--"

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:36.501
I'm like, "No! No, no!" I know. Well, bec-- Yeah.

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:39.133
I mean, one year, actually, on season two of "Stranger Things,"

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:41.868
all us kids went together but as different things.

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:44.634
I was Harley Quinn, and Finn was a whoopie cushion.

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:46.200
It was the funniest thing.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.934
And everybody turned up on the -- Ding, dong!

00:06:47.934 --> 00:06:49.467
Trick or treat!

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:51.200
"Stranger Things" kids? The whole thing.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.267
-Yeah, 'cause everyone together. You're like, "Oh, boy."

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:54.968
-Yeah, it's not really happening, but it is.

00:06:54.968 --> 00:06:56.334
-When the Beatles travel together,

00:06:56.334 --> 00:06:57.534
they're still Beatles, yeah.

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.767
What can we say? What is "Enola Holmes 2"?

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:01.234
What's happening in this movie?

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:05.501
-So, this time around we indulge in a real story

00:07:05.501 --> 00:07:08.567
about matchstick girls, and they --

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:10.000
It's a real strike

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.534
that was led in late 1800s by Sarah Chapman.

00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:16.400
And we get to really uncover that mystery

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.334
as to why these girls were being treated so badly.

00:07:19.334 --> 00:07:20.934
-Boy, I love that. -Yes.

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:23.968
And I think it's really great because it is shining a light

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:27.767
on female workers and protecting them and their rights,

00:07:27.767 --> 00:07:30.667
and it's an amazing story, and obviously you get to

00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:33.100
go along with it with her video camera,

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.901
her video diary I say.

00:07:34.901 --> 00:07:36.701
Enola's video diary. "Hey, guys!"

00:07:36.701 --> 00:07:38.300
She's like a blogger on YouTube.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.534
-Yeah, basically -- Just talking to camera.

00:07:40.534 --> 00:07:43.467
-Go along with Enola and figure it out.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:45.267
-You crush it. I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:45.267 --> 00:07:47.367
Here's Millie Bobby Brown in "Enola Holmes 2."

00:07:47.367 --> 00:07:49.300
Take a look at this.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.334
-Whoo!

00:07:50.334 --> 00:07:51.534
-[ Thud ] -Ugh!

00:07:51.534 --> 00:07:52.968
-My mistake.

00:07:52.968 --> 00:07:55.334
I should have warned you I was opening it.

00:07:57.567 --> 00:07:59.000
-Don't. No.

00:08:04.267 --> 00:08:05.767
-Dare I ask?

00:08:05.767 --> 00:08:09.267
♪♪

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:12.267
-Aah! [ Gasps ]

00:08:12.267 --> 00:08:13.701
Good afternoon.

00:08:13.701 --> 00:08:15.634
May I ask a favor?

00:08:15.634 --> 00:08:20.767
♪♪

00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:23.367
-Never mind. Tell me everything.

00:08:23.367 --> 00:08:25.634
[ Cheers and applause ] -Yeah! That's right.

00:08:25.634 --> 00:08:27.300
Millie Bobby Brown, everyone.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:31.567
"Enola Holmes 2" is available on Netflix November 4th.

00:08:31.567 --> 00:08:34.334
Michael Imperioli joins us next. Stick around, everybody.

00:08:34.334 --> 00:08:36.634
Hi, Eeyore! Go to sleep!

